ssage": "Create  README.md\n\nA simple text editor application with basic features created using Tkinter in Python.", "created_at": "2023-11-19T17:50:01Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "9d090defa0797d094fa1662ead3e9a4bb6cd6330", "message": "Create README.md\n\nA simple command-line TO-DO list application where you can add, remove, and view tasks.", "created_at": "2023-11-19T17:48:22Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3e84f3945b55956d9331762855cda2ed5cd80bf7", "message": "Create README.md\n\nA simple Python script that uses the Fixer API to convert currencies based on the latest exchange rates.", "created_at": "2023-11-19T17:46:22Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "241fdeb98151edb9376799172882760bdd2bb490", "message": "Create README.md\n\nA simple guessing game where the player tries to guess a randomly generated number between 1 and 10.", "created_at": "2023-11-19T17:43:42Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3f9ea1647e8533ab99ff2c0c4e5f25845cf36b8f", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2023-11-19T17:40:21Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1cd8419cb1ee359eb01e38130b2ab1a60411df5d", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2023-11-18T23:07:34Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "622d04c5b0184eaa62ec5ae61a2920dd919aa724", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2023-11-18T23:00:59Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a1e2ef752f4b6a2315e51027a5692fcce955272a", "message": " README.md\n\nBuilding a weather forecast app using Python and Tkinter showcases the power of programming in delivering practical solutions. The application provides users with real-time weather information for any desired location, empowering them to make informed decisions based on current weather conditions. The user-friendly GUI and error handling mechanisms enhance the overall usability and reliability of the app. By combining the capabilities of Python, Tkinter, and the OpenWeatherMap API, developers can create versatile weather forecast applications that cater to the needs of users worldwide.", "created_at": "2023-11-18T22:49:16Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "126ec877c33e1adde221748f2abccbdd2b6bfc3d", "message": "Building a Weather Forecast App with Tkinter.\n\nIntroduction:\r\nIn today's fast-paced world, having access to accurate weather information is crucial. With the advancements in technology, creating a weather forecast application using Python and Tkinter has become a popular project for both beginners and experienced programmers. This essay explores the development process of a weather forecast app using Python and Tkinter, highlighting its key features and functionality.\r\n\r\nProject Overview:\r\nThe weather forecast app is designed to provide users with real-time weather information for a given location. It utilizes the OpenWeatherMap API to fetch weather data, including temperature, humidity, wind speed, pressure, and precipitation. The application has a user-friendly graphical user interface (GUI) built using Tkinter, a popular Python GUI framework.\r\n\r\nGUI Design:\r\nThe GUI of the weather forecast app is clean and intuitive, ensuring a seamless user experience. It consists of a main window with various elements organized in a grid layout. The key elements include:\r\n\r\n1. Location Label: Displays the text \"Location\" to prompt the user for input.\r\n2. Location Entry: Allows the user to enter the desired location.\r\n3. Search Button: Triggers the weather data retrieval process.\r\n4. Temperature Label: Displays the current temperature in Celsius.\r\n5. Humidity Label: Displays the current humidity percentage.\r\n6. Wind Speed Label: Displays the current wind speed in kilometers per hour.\r\n7. Pressure Label: Displays the current atmospheric pressure in hectopascals.\r\n8. Precipitation Label: Displays the current precipitation percentage.\r\n\r\nFunctionality:\r\nThe weather forecast app retrieves weather data based on the user's input. When the user enters a location and clicks the \"Search\" button, the application sends a request to the OpenWeatherMap API using the provided location and API key. It then receives the weather data in JSON format. The app extracts the relevant information from the JSON response and updates the corresponding labels on the GUI with the fetched data, including temperature, humidity, wind speed, pressure, and precipitation.\r\n\r\nError Handling:\r\nThe weather forecast app incorporates error handling to ensure a robust user experience. If the user fails to provide a location before clicking the \"Search\" button, a message box appears with a prompt to enter a location. Additionally, if an error occurs during the API request or data extraction process, an informative message box displays the encountered error, allowing the user to understand the issue.\r\n\r\nConclusion:\r\nBuilding a weather forecast app using Python and Tkinter showcases the power of programming in delivering practical solutions. The application provides users with real-time weather information for any desired location, empowering them to make informed decisions based on current weather conditions. The user-friendly GUI and error handling mechanisms enhance the overall usability and reliability of the app. By combining the capabilities of Python, Tkinter, and the OpenWeatherMap API, developers can create versatile weather forecast applications that cater to the needs of users worldwide.", "created_at": "2023-11-18T22:45:47Z", "repo": "Python_Projects", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "dfdeb56563600bff1f5b41f89ccb657f9113aaef", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-12-10T16:25:47Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "1d5715fa60a3f519c98c779c76fcdb42b4ab7083", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-12-10T16:24:43Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "21a74e7d69a6ea6aa1508a9b101e97bb6f6023a3", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-12-10T16:24:02Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2ea89dee4c89243fc910175cf1a6f0914e84805f", "message": "Rename UI 1.jpeg to UI_1.jpeg", "created_at": "2023-12-10T16:23:43Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "4ba40f1a3bac6f79d0163073d37ffe21b9be4c91", "message": "Rename UI 2.png to UI_2.png", "created_at": "2023-12-10T16:23:22Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "3ee6b653384399610aa2d9f48a262e9e127a2758", "message": "Add files via upload", "created_at": "2023-11-24T07:09:35Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "a354bafe650b9450b1c8c5d47338a8351f5245c0", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-11-24T07:03:21Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "7a41d4aeecd55f24ae63c3211b3d5af816383cfa", "message": "Update README.md\n\n\r\nThe Weather Forecast App is a Python-based application that provides real-time weather information for a given location. It utilizes the OpenWeatherMap API to fetch weather data and presents it in a user-friendly graphical user interface (GUI) built with Tkinter.", "created_at": "2023-11-24T07:02:25Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "2db4ffb0e1d8ea4da6109ac6385a40453c4fcfb4", "message": "Update README.md", "created_at": "2023-11-24T06:56:01Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}, {"sha": "29e3983231034363b17628ff419698df6e9a9a70", "message": "Initial commit", "created_at": "2023-11-24T06:55:22Z", "repo": "Weather-App", "file_sampled": false, "has_test_file": null, "has_impl_file": null}], "prs": []}